.TH "BARMAN-CHECK-BACKUP" "1" "Nov 17, 2026" "3.21" "Barman"
.SH NAME
barman-check-backup \- Barman Sub-Commands
.SH SYNOPSIS
.INDENT 0.0
.INDENT 3.5
.sp
.EX
check\-backup
    [ { \-h | \-\-help } ]
    SERVER_NAME BACKUP_ID
.EE
.UNINDENT
.UNINDENT
.SH DESCRIPTION
.sp
Check that all necessary WAL files for verifying the consistency of a physical backup are
properly archived. This command is automatically executed by the cron job and at the end
of each backup operation. You can use a backup name or a
shortcut instead of \fBBACKUP_ID\fP\&.
.sp
The exit status reflects the status of the backup after the check:
.TS
box center;
l|l.
T{
\fBExit code\fP
T}	T{
\fBMeaning\fP
T}
_
T{
\fB0\fP
T}	T{
The backup is \fBDONE\fP: all the required WAL files are archived.
T}
_
T{
\fB1\fP
T}	T{
The backup is not \fBDONE\fP, or the check could not be performed. This happens
when:
.INDENT 0.0
.IP \(bu 2
The backup is \fBFAILED\fP, for example because a required WAL file is missing.
.IP \(bu 2
The backup is \fBWAITING_FOR_WALS\fP: not all the required WAL files have been
archived yet, so the backup consistency cannot be verified.
.IP \(bu 2
The check could not be performed, for example because another process holds
the backup lock.
.UNINDENT
T}
.TE
.SH PARAMETERS
.INDENT 0.0
.TP
.B \fBSERVER_NAME\fP
Name of the server in barman node.
.TP
.B \fBBACKUP_ID\fP
ID or name of the backup in the barman catalog. If more than one backup has the
same name, the command fails and lists the matching backup IDs.
.TP
.B \fB\-h\fP / \fB\-\-help\fP
Show a help message and exit. Provides information about command usage.
.UNINDENT
.SH SHORTCUTS
.sp
Use shortcuts instead of \fBBACKUP_ID\fP\&.
.TS
box center;
l|l.
T{
\fBShortcut\fP
T}	T{
\fBDescription\fP
T}
_
T{
\fBfirst/oldest\fP
T}	T{
Oldest available backup for the server, in chronological order.
T}
_
T{
\fBlast/latest\fP
T}	T{
Most recent available backup for the server, in chronological order.
T}
_
T{
\fBlast\-full/latest\-full\fP
T}	T{
Most recent full backup taken with methods \fBrsync\fP or \fBpostgres\fP\&.
T}
_
T{
\fBlast\-failed\fP
T}	T{
Most recent backup that failed, in chronological order.
T}
.TE
